<<~ ahu slot=`#/sol-handwright-lares`>>

! Sol-Handwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

Lares (Ink-Clerk), Lares (Council), Lares (Artificer): ''✶ Observe.'' I re-read both hands and the carriers. One end state holds: ''the session carries the hand''. “A session wears the face and the vessel wears none” (`stable-founding-road.mem:106-107`); “Every hand that reaches a vessel opens a session” and “The door carries; the hand authorizes” (`session-contract.mem:61,85`). Node and browser carry the same model, with platform-specific ports. K15 bonds lands before identity hunks; D2 owns the TW5 island/port and projection gate; I2 keeps its separately scouted relay lane. All identity, receipt and authorship bytes land before the bake.

''⏿ Orient — H1, one cut.'' I accept ''four hands lanes plus I2'', but move the boundaries from my wave one. F4/F5 receipts belong to ''session authority and outcomes'', since a one-shot caller dies while the same verified face must recover its outcome (`session-contract.mem:186-206`); an authored-records lane would ship a temporary receipt reader. P13 belongs to ''surface mount'', since one resolver combines face grant, recipe and profile at mount and a recipe cannot widen a grant (`session-contract.mem:152-162`; `surface-recipe.ts:75-105,174-175`). B2 belongs to ''holder and surfaces'': two tabs need separate islands over one Repo, so splitting the proof into a later device lane would leave the holder's ownership model unfinished (`session-contract.mem:126-144,221-223`; `shared-holder-core.ts:578-594`). F12 authored records follows the session signer, while F10 device view follows the face relation. G13 dispatch follows verified author and durable outcomes. I2 follows I1 and its own scout.

''H2, first move now — DERIVED (build the end state; one name, one relation).'' The first lane may start ''now'', on files K15 and D2 do not hold: `packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-contract.ts`, `session-document-view.ts`, `surface-recipe.ts`, `wiki-recipe.ts` (working-slot resolution); `packages/lararium-node/src/uds-channel.ts`; `packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-vm.ts`; and their focused proof files. First slice: define one binding from socket/port to owner epoch, session id, generation, verified face reference and fixed hand profile; make UDS refuse copied socket, wrong face and stale generation, then bind request digest/outcome lookup to the face proof subject. The existing UDS ledger holds durable outcomes but its socket opens no verified face (`session-contract.mem:279,297`; `uds-channel.ts:639-646`); `verb-vm.ts:114,162,169,220` still passes caller `requestedBy`. Keep the supplier/signature adapter seam explicit; merge K15's atom and opener hunks once landed. Do ''not'' edit `keyhive-provider`, `place-card`, `ceremony-core`, `boot-daemon-keyhive`, `carriage-relay`, `carriage-caps`, `node-caps`, either vessel opener, or D2's TW5 island/port, `hand-gate.ts`, `tw5-projection.ts`, `projection-sink.ts` in this first slice. A lane may start; its production face-open proof waits for K15 and its surface integration waits for D2. No interim vessel selector ships.

''◇ Decide — H3, OPERATOR.'' Options: ''(a)'' open one live session for `(PersonaGroup, Nexus)`; ''(b)'' open one PersonaGroup session with separately bounded Nexus facets. Lean ''(a)''. Canon fixes one face per session, yet explicitly withholds the two-Nexus word (`session-contract.mem:295`; `face-proof.mem:297`). The proof key and admit bind `(PersonaGroup,Nexus)`, and the signer binds `(session,Nexus)` (`face-proof.mem:45-47,64-66`); a dial takes one `(hearth,Nexus)` path (`stable-founding-road.mem:728`). The effective recipe freezes for a session's mount (`session-contract.mem:154-158`), and cabal/realm grants narrow by relation (`session-contract.mem:238`; `cabal-realm.ts:54-64`). These facts favor (a), but do not forbid (b); the two facets could each carry their own proof and recipe. Ask the operator for this one architectural choice before freezing the session face type.

''H4, the person's joints.'' ''CANON:'' `persona wear` switches the caller's ''live'' session, not a later CLI invocation (`session-contract.mem:198-206`); the five-step fence advances its generation and leaves sibling sessions alone (`:257-265`). Thus no close-and-open substitute. ''CANON:'' the receipt rests with proof subject plus input digest; a later same-face session reads it, another face cannot (`:186-190`). ''DERIVED (causal islands; one name, one relation):'' the display must identify request/action, verified face, outcome or unknown, and causal position/last verified fence; `requestedBy` remains display text (`:190,204`; `uds-channel.ts:639-646`). Exact typography needs no operator ruling. ''CANON:'' a wall clock cannot decide an act (`stable-founding-road.mem:112`); observed causal revocation closes dependent sessions, while incomplete history says incomplete (`session-contract.mem:246-249`). ''DERIVED (no global now):'' show the long-silent device's last verified fence and allow explicit removal; never invent expiry. The road still lists a broader long-silent-device lean (`stable-founding-road.mem:853`), but this hands lane needs no threshold to enforce removal.

''▶ Act — ordered whole lanes; each slice runs red → control → known positive.''

# ''Session authority, switch and outcomes:'' F3/F4/F5/F9/A8/W17. Hold mesh `session-contract.ts`, `session-face.ts`, `session-signer.ts`, `wiki-recipe.ts` working resolver; node `uds-channel.ts`, TW5 `verb-vm.ts`, CLI `persona` callers, then node/browser opener session hunks. Red: copied socket, cross-face receipt, stale generation, wrong working address. Control: same-face later CLI recovers receipt; sibling session survives switch. Positive: K15-selected atom signs and one live session switches through all five steps. K15 opener identity hunks land first; this lane owns receipt format and working-address genesis before bake.
# ''Scoped surface and holder:'' F1/F2/F6/P13/B2. Hold mesh `session-document-view.ts`, `surface-recipe.ts`, pool `mountSurface`; node/browser compose/mount callers; browser `shared-holder-core.ts` and runtime; TW5 view port after D2. Red: foreign document/catalog fetch, cross-tab reply, two Repos. Control: allowed same-face read, same-face tabs separate. Positive: two faces/tabs, one holder, two bounded islands and recipes. Merge D2 port/gate first and K15 opener supplier; recipe/grant bytes settle before bake.
# ''Hands, fleet and authorship:'' F10/F11/F12. Hold watcher/projector, MCP seat adapter, fleet view/removal, `parallel-drafts.ts` and shared-record writer. Red: unleased disk edit signs, spoofed `modifier` authors, stale removed device acts. Control: leased edit, standing-seat draft, retained device. Positive: signed face authorship plus Mask as non-authorizing field, causal fleet removal and catch-up. Consume D2 projection and K15 face signer; authorship/fleet bytes precede bake.
# ''Intent and effects:'' G13. Hold `verb-summons.ts`, `verb-dispatcher.ts`, effect ledger/reader and intent adapter. Red: forged writer, wrong audience, replay after restart, canon tombstone. Control: authorized fresh intent. Positive: working-only tombstone, durable lease/fence and result. Consume I1 face plane, lane-one receipt and signer; effect bytes precede bake.
# ''I2 relay:'' independent scouted lane after I1, K15 and session signer. Hold delegation/revoke, intent entry/reader, relay admission and seat. Red: altered arguments or revoked grant; control: valid local act; positive: far agent reaches its intended face device with relay recording transit only (`/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/i2-relay/sol/out.md:17-22`). Its grant bytes precede bake.

''↺ Aftermath.'' One operator joint remains: the two-Nexus session shape. The first isolated slice can start while K15 and D2 finish; the lanes integrate in the order above.

